<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Æthelwealh of Sussex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 685</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Æthelwealh was king of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> in the later 7th century and the first Christian king of Sussex. Baptised in Mercia with King Wulfhere as his sponsor, he received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isle-of-wight">Isle of Wight</a> and the Meon valley from him, and gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfrid">Wilfrid</a> land at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selsey">Selsey</a> to found a monastery. He was killed around 685 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caedwalla">Cædwalla of Wessex</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelwealh-of-sussex.jpg" alt="Æthelwealh of Sussex" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ethelwolfe_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
